{"name":"Animal Kingdom","hex":"#bcc09e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"animal kingdom","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The regnum Animalia; the set of all animals."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/animal_kingdom"}],"entries":[{"title":"Animal","blocks":[{"text":"Animals are multicellular, eukaryotic organisms belonging to the biological kingdom Animalia. Animals consume organic material, breathe oxygen, have muscle cells, can reproduce sexually, and grow from a hollow sphere of cells, the blastula, during embryonic development. With few exceptions, animals are able to move. Animals form a clade, meaning that they arose from a single common ancestor. Over 1.5 million living animal species have been described, of which around 1.05 million are insects, over 85,000 are molluscs, and around 65,000 are vertebrates. It has been estimated there are as many as 7.77 million animal species on Earth. Animal body lengths range from 8.5 μm (0.00033 in) to 33.6 m (110 ft). They have complex ecologies and interactions with each other and their environments, forming intricate food webs. The scientific study of animals is known as zoology, and the study of animal behaviour is known as ethology."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Animal_diversity_b.png/330px-Animal_diversity_b.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Animal"},{"title":"Animal Kingdom (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Animal Kingdom is a champion American Thoroughbred racehorse who won the 2011 Kentucky Derby and 2013 Dubai World Cup."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Animal_Kingdom_%282008%29.jpg/330px-Animal_Kingdom_%282008%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Animal_Kingdom_(horse)"},{"title":"Animal Kingdom (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Animal Kingdom is an American crime drama television series developed by Jonathan Lisco. It is based on the 2010 Australian film of the same name, which in turn was inspired by the criminal Pettingill family. The series was produced by David Michôd, who wrote and directed the original film."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Animal_Kingdom_logo.png/330px-Animal_Kingdom_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Animal_Kingdom_(TV_series)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Blastulation.png/500px-Blastulation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Blastulation.png/500px-Blastulation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Animals are unique in having the ball of cells of the early embryo (1) develop into a hollow ball or blastula (2).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlastulation.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Odonata_copulation.jpg/500px-Odonata_copulation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Odonata_copulation.jpg/1280px-Odonata_copulation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Odonata_copulation.jpg/500px-Odonata_copulation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sexual reproduction is nearly universal in animals, such as these dragonflies.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOdonata_copulation.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Ultramarine_Flycatcher_%28Ficedula_superciliaris%29_Naggar%2C_Himachal_Pradesh%2C_2013_%28cropped%29.JPG/500px-Ultramari